// © scriptmasterlabs — SML CVD Regime Desk (Pine Script v6)
// Corrected build of the operator-submitted "CVD Regime Fast → Call/Put Desk"
// script (submitted 2026-07-30). Indicator only — draws signals, does not
// backtest. Python twin (single source of truth): cvd_regime_engine.py.
//
// BACKTEST VERDICT — READ THIS BEFORE TRADING IT: NO DEMONSTRATED EDGE. Real
// 5-minute bars, SPY/QQQ/IWM/NVDA/TSLA, 2026-07-20..29 (8 sessions): 102 trades,
// 41.2% win rate, profit factor 0.989, -0.30% summed, 4 of 5 symbols lost money.
// Method, sensitivity runs, limitations: docs/CVD_REGIME_BACKTEST_2026-07-30.md
// Fixing the seven bugs below made this script CORRECT. It did not make it
// profitable. Use it to watch regime and conviction, not as a proven signal.
//
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// WHAT WAS BROKEN IN THE SUBMITTED SCRIPT — 7 real bugs. Every number below was
// MEASURED by reproducing the original formula in
// tests/test_cvd_regime_engine_smoke.py, not estimated.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 1. CRITICAL — HTF slope was indexed on CHART bars, not HTF bars:
//        htfCvdS  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTF, cvdS)
//        htfSlope = htfCvdS - htfCvdS[slopeLen]
//    request.security() holds the last CLOSED higher-timeframe value flat
//    across every chart bar inside the forming HTF bar. On a 5-min chart with a
//    60-min HTF that is 12 identical bars, so htfCvdS - htfCvdS[3] == 0.0 on 9
//    of every 12 bars — measured at 73.7% of bars. On those bars htfBull and
//    htfBear were BOTH false, and alignedBull/alignedBear/earlyCall/earlyPut all
//    require one of them, so no signal of any kind could fire there.
//    The effect was signal QUANTIZATION, not starvation: every signal the script
//    could produce was confined to the 26.4% of bars where an HTF boundary fell
//    inside the 3-bar window — a short burst after each hourly close — and on
//    those bars it read a 1-HTF-BAR difference, never the intended 3. Measured on
//    the same real bars, the original emitted MORE signals than the fixed engine
//    (217 vs 102 across 5 symbols), because bugs 2 and 5 left it with no working
//    conviction gate and no position state. Timing and lookback were the problem,
//    not signal volume.
//    FIX: the HTF series is built natively from bar timestamps and its slope is
//    measured in HTF space. request.security() is gone entirely — which also
//    removes its realtime-repaint behaviour and guarantees this chart matches
//    cvd_regime_engine.py exactly.
// 2. The conviction filter did nothing. Flat ±14/±10/±10 contributions off a
//    base of 50 meant an aligned-bull bar always scored ≥84 and an aligned-bear
//    bar always ≤16, so "score >= minConviction" (default 55) and
//    "score <= 100 - minConviction" were always true whenever alignment held.
//    minConviction was a no-op for any value from 17 to 83.
//    FIX: contributions are continuous (magnitude-scaled), so a weakly-aligned
//    bar scores near 50 and the threshold actually binds.
// 3. strength was dimensionally wrong: abs(3-bar CVD CHANGE) / stdev(CVD LEVEL).
//    With a daily reset the level's stdev dwarfs a 3-bar change, so the ratio was
//    systematically depressed — measured median 0.326, hitting the
//    math.min(strength*7, 14) cap on only 1.5% of bars. The term contributed ~2
//    of a possible 14 points almost always, so it could not tell a violent flow
//    impulse from a drifting one — the whole reason it exists.
//    FIX: the slope is normalized by the rolling stdev of the SLOPE (median 0.948).
// 4. cvd was reset daily but ta.ema(cvd, smoothLen) was NOT, so the smoothed
//    series carried the prior session's ending level into each new session — a
//    large artificial slope on the first bars of every day, in whichever
//    direction yesterday closed.
//    FIX: the EMA state is re-seeded on reset, the slope window is cleared, and
//    no signal is allowed until slopeLen bars into the session.
// 5. exitLong/exitShort were neither position-aware nor edge-gated — an X-cross
//    plotted on every bar of a trend, firing whether or not anything was open.
//    FIX: a real one-position-at-a-time state machine.
// 6. No barstate.isconfirmed anywhere → shapes and alerts could fire mid-bar
//    and then vanish. Every other v6 script in indicators/ confirms on close.
//    FIX: bar-close confirmation on every signal and alert.
// 7. No risk container at all on a script whose stated purpose is buying
//    options. FIX: ATR stop, R-multiple target, post-exit cooldown.
//
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DISCLOSURES — read these before believing any number on this chart
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// • "CVD" here is a BAR-RANGE PROXY for delta computed from ordinary OHLCV:
//   volume * ((close-low) - (high-close)) / (high-low). It is NOT true bid/ask
//   delta — that needs tick/quote data TradingView's standard feed does not
//   provide to an indicator. Same proxy class as the OFI/DLMD labelling in
//   SML_Cycle_Intelligence_Engine_v6.pine.
// • The stop and target are modelled on the UNDERLYING's directional move. They
//   do NOT model option premium, leverage, theta or spread. A profitable
//   directional read is necessary but NOT sufficient for profitable options.
// • This script does not size positions and does not know your account.
//
//@version=6
indicator("SML CVD Regime Desk", overlay=false, max_bars_back=1000, precision=0)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
grpCore = "Core"
resetPeriod   = input.string("Day", "CVD Reset", options=["None", "Day", "Week", "Month"], group=grpCore)
smoothLen     = input.int(5, "CVD Smoothing (lower = faster)", minval=1, group=grpCore)
slopeLen      = input.int(3, "Slope Lookback (lower = faster)", minval=1, group=grpCore)
stdevLen      = input.int(30, "Strength Normalization Window", minval=5, group=grpCore, tooltip="Rolling window used to normalize the CVD slope into sigma units. The slope is divided by the stdev of the SLOPE (not of the CVD level — that was a bug in the original script).")

grpAdv = "Filters"
htfMin        = input.int(60, "Higher Timeframe (minutes)", minval=1, group=grpAdv, tooltip="Now a plain minute count, not a timeframe string: the HTF flow series is built natively from bar timestamps so its slope is measured in HTF bars. The original used request.security() and indexed the slope across CHART bars, which made it exactly 0 on ~74% of bars (no signal possible there) and a 1-hour-bar difference on the rest — so signals could only appear in a burst after each hourly close, on the wrong lookback.")
emaLen        = input.int(13, "Price Filter EMA", minval=1, group=grpAdv)
minConviction = input.int(55, "Min Conviction", minval=0, maxval=100, group=grpAdv)
useEarly      = input.bool(true, "Show Early Signals (price allowed to lag)", group=grpAdv)
earlySlack    = input.int(8, "Early Signal Slack", minval=0, maxval=25, group=grpAdv)

grpRisk = "Risk (per-trade container)"
atrLen        = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval=1, group=grpRisk)
stopAtr       = input.float(1.5, "Stop Distance (ATR)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpRisk)
targetR       = input.float(2.0, "Target (R multiple of stop)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group=grpRisk)
cooldownBars  = input.int(3, "Cooldown After Exit (bars)", minval=0, group=grpRisk)
exitOnFlip    = input.bool(true, "Exit When Flow Regime Flips", group=grpRisk)

grpVis = "Visuals"
showBg        = input.bool(true, "Regime Background", group=grpVis)
showTable     = input.bool(true, "Desk Dashboard", group=grpVis)

grpWebhook = "SqueezeOS Webhook Bridge"
whPass        = input.string("", "Webhook Passphrase", group=grpWebhook, tooltip="STEP 1 of 2: type any password here (make one up). This box is empty by default, so NO signals are sent until you fill it in. STEP 2: copy that exact same password into the TV_WEBHOOK_PASSPHRASE environment variable on the squeezeos-api Render service, then create ONE TradingView alert on this indicator with Condition = 'Any alert() function call' and paste https://squeezeos-api.onrender.com/api/webhooks/tradingview into the Webhook URL field. Leave the alert's Message box untouched — this script builds the JSON itself.")

// Weights sum to 50, so a fully-aligned max-strength bar reaches exactly 100.
float W_FLOW  = 20.0
float W_HTF   = 18.0
float W_PRICE = 12.0
float DIV_PEN = 16.0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CVD ENGINE — reset-aware, with re-seeded smoothing (BUG 4 fix)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float rng      = high - low
float barDelta = rng > 0 ? volume * ((close - low) - (high - close)) / rng : 0.0

bool doReset = switch resetPeriod
    "Day"   => ta.change(time("D")) != 0
    "Week"  => ta.change(time("W")) != 0
    "Month" => ta.change(time("M")) != 0
    => false
doReset := bar_index > 0 and doReset

// resetId identifies the current CVD session. Carried alongside the HTF series
// so an HTF slope is never measured ACROSS a reset.
var int resetId = 0
if doReset
    resetId += 1

var float cvd = 0.0
cvd := doReset ? barDelta : nz(cvd[1]) + barDelta

// Manual EMA so the state can be re-seeded on reset (ta.ema cannot be reset).
var float cvdS = na
float kCvd = 2.0 / (smoothLen + 1.0)
cvdS := doReset or na(cvdS) ? barDelta : cvdS + kCvd * (cvd - cvdS)

var int barsSinceReset = 0
barsSinceReset := doReset ? 1 : barsSinceReset + 1

// ── chart-timeframe flow slope, reset-aware ────────────────────
var smoothArr = array.new<float>()
var slopeArr  = array.new<float>()
if doReset
    array.clear(smoothArr)
    array.clear(slopeArr)
array.push(smoothArr, cvdS)
if array.size(smoothArr) > slopeLen + 1
    array.shift(smoothArr)
float cvdSlope = array.size(smoothArr) > slopeLen ? cvdS - array.get(smoothArr, array.size(smoothArr) - 1 - slopeLen) : 0.0
array.push(slopeArr, cvdSlope)
if array.size(slopeArr) > stdevLen
    array.shift(slopeArr)
float sdSlope = array.size(slopeArr) > 1 ? array.stdev(slopeArr, false) : 0.0
float flowN   = sdSlope > 0 ? math.max(-1.0, math.min(1.0, cvdSlope / sdSlope)) : 0.0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HTF FLOW — built natively from timestamps (BUG 1 fix)
// Only COMPLETED higher-timeframe buckets are ever read, so this is causal and
// cannot repaint. No request.security() anywhere.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var htfVals   = array.new<float>()   // smoothed CVD at each completed HTF close
var htfKeys   = array.new<int>()     // resetId that HTF bucket belonged to
var htfSlopes = array.new<float>()   // slope samples, for normalization

// Largest lag ≤ slopeLen whose bucket is in the SAME session as the latest.
// Walking the lag down (instead of blanking the read) keeps the first ~3 hours
// of every session tradeable with a 60-minute HTF, while never comparing
// post-reset CVD against pre-reset CVD.
f_ssSlope() =>
    float res = na
    int n = array.size(htfVals)
    if n >= 2
        int   lk   = array.get(htfKeys, n - 1)
        float lv   = array.get(htfVals, n - 1)
        int   best = 0
        for L = 1 to slopeLen
            if n > L and array.get(htfKeys, n - 1 - L) == lk
                best := L
        if best > 0
            res := lv - array.get(htfVals, n - 1 - best)
    res

int htfBucket = int(math.floor(time / (htfMin * 60000)))
var int   curHtfBucket  = na
var float curHtfLast    = na
var int   curHtfResetId = na

if na(curHtfBucket)
    curHtfBucket := htfBucket
else if htfBucket != curHtfBucket
    // the previous HTF bucket just CLOSED — only now is it usable
    if not na(curHtfLast)
        array.push(htfVals, curHtfLast)
        array.push(htfKeys, curHtfResetId)
        if array.size(htfVals) > slopeLen + 2
            array.shift(htfVals)
            array.shift(htfKeys)
        float smp = f_ssSlope()
        if not na(smp)
            array.push(htfSlopes, smp)
            if array.size(htfSlopes) > stdevLen
                array.shift(htfSlopes)
    curHtfBucket := htfBucket
curHtfLast    := cvdS
curHtfResetId := resetId

float htfSlope = na
bool  haveHtf  = false
if array.size(htfVals) > 0 and array.get(htfKeys, array.size(htfVals) - 1) == resetId
    float s = f_ssSlope()
    if not na(s)
        htfSlope := s
        haveHtf  := true
float sdHtf = array.size(htfSlopes) > 1 ? array.stdev(htfSlopes, false) : 0.0
float htfN  = haveHtf and sdHtf > 0 ? math.max(-1.0, math.min(1.0, htfSlope / sdHtf)) : 0.0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PRICE FILTER + ATR (manual, to match cvd_regime_engine.py exactly)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float emaPx = na
float kPx = 2.0 / (emaLen + 1.0)
emaPx := na(emaPx) ? close : emaPx + kPx * (close - emaPx)

var float atrV = na
float tr = na(close[1]) ? high - low : math.max(high - low, math.max(math.abs(high - close[1]), math.abs(low - close[1])))
atrV := na(atrV) ? tr : atrV + (tr - atrV) / atrLen

float priceN = atrV > 0 ? math.max(-1.0, math.min(1.0, (close - emaPx) / atrV)) : 0.0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// REGIME + CONVICTION (BUG 2 + BUG 3 fix — the threshold now binds)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
bool alignedBull = flowN > 0 and priceN > 0 and htfN > 0
bool alignedBear = flowN < 0 and priceN < 0 and htfN < 0
bool divergence  = (flowN > 0 and priceN < 0) or (flowN < 0 and priceN > 0)

string regime = alignedBull ? "ALIGNED BULL" : alignedBear ? "ALIGNED BEAR" : divergence ? "DIVERGENCE" : "NEUTRAL"

float score = 50.0 + W_FLOW * flowN + W_HTF * htfN + W_PRICE * priceN - (divergence ? DIV_PEN : 0.0)
score := math.max(0.0, math.min(100.0, score))
float strength = math.abs(flowN)

// No signal until the slope window is honest for this session AND an HTF
// confirmation genuinely exists.
bool warm = barsSinceReset > slopeLen and haveHtf and array.size(slopeArr) > slopeLen

float putThresh = 100.0 - minConviction
bool callOk   = warm and alignedBull and score >= minConviction
bool putOk    = warm and alignedBear and score <= putThresh
bool earlyCall = warm and useEarly and not callOk and flowN > 0 and htfN > 0 and score >= minConviction - earlySlack
bool earlyPut  = warm and useEarly and not putOk  and flowN < 0 and htfN < 0 and score <= putThresh + earlySlack

bool wantLong  = callOk or earlyCall
bool wantShort = putOk or earlyPut
string bias = callOk ? "CALL" : putOk ? "PUT" : earlyCall ? "EARLY CALL" : earlyPut ? "EARLY PUT" : "WAIT"

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// POSITION STATE MACHINE (BUG 5 + BUG 6 + BUG 7 fix)
// One position at a time. Every transition is evaluated only on a confirmed
// bar close, so nothing repaints.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int   posDir     = 0        // 1 long, -1 short, 0 flat
var float entryPx    = na
var float stopPx     = na
var float targetPx   = na
var int   cooldown   = 0

bool evEnterLong  = false
bool evEnterShort = false
bool evExitStop   = false
bool evExitTarget = false
bool evExitFlip   = false

if barstate.isconfirmed
    if posDir != 0
        bool hitStop   = posDir == 1 ? close <= stopPx   : close >= stopPx
        bool hitTarget = posDir == 1 ? close >= targetPx : close <= targetPx
        bool flipped   = exitOnFlip and (posDir == 1 ? wantShort : wantLong)
        if hitStop
            evExitStop := true
        else if hitTarget
            evExitTarget := true
        else if flipped
            evExitFlip := true
        if evExitStop or evExitTarget or evExitFlip
            posDir   := 0
            entryPx  := na
            stopPx   := na
            targetPx := na
            cooldown := cooldownBars
    else if cooldown > 0
        cooldown -= 1
    else if atrV > 0
        if wantLong
            posDir      := 1
            entryPx     := close
            stopPx      := close - stopAtr * atrV
            targetPx    := close + stopAtr * atrV * targetR
            evEnterLong := true
        else if wantShort
            posDir       := -1
            entryPx      := close
            stopPx       := close + stopAtr * atrV
            targetPx     := close - stopAtr * atrV * targetR
            evEnterShort := true

bool evExit = evExitStop or evExitTarget or evExitFlip

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLOTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plot(cvdS, "CVD Fast (proxy)", color=#FF9800, linewidth=2)
hline(0, "Zero", color=color.new(#546E7A, 70), linestyle=hline.style_dashed)

bgcolor(showBg ? (alignedBull ? color.new(#00C853, 91) :
                  alignedBear ? color.new(#FF1744, 91) :
                  divergence  ? color.new(#AA00FF, 93) : na) : na)

// Confirmed entries — full conviction
plotshape(evEnterLong and callOk, title="CALL", style=shape.triangleup, location=location.bottom, color=#00C853, size=size.normal, text="CALL")
plotshape(evEnterShort and putOk, title="PUT", style=shape.triangledown, location=location.top, color=#FF1744, size=size.normal, text="PUT")
// Confirmed entries — early (price lagging)
plotshape(evEnterLong and not callOk, title="Early CALL", style=shape.triangleup, location=location.bottom, color=color.new(#00C853, 40), size=size.small, text="early")
plotshape(evEnterShort and not putOk, title="Early PUT", style=shape.triangledown, location=location.top, color=color.new(#FF1744, 40), size=size.small, text="early")
// Exits — only ever plotted when a position was actually open
plotshape(evExitTarget, title="Exit Target", style=shape.xcross, location=location.bottom, color=#00E5FF, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(evExitStop,   title="Exit Stop",   style=shape.xcross, location=location.top,    color=#FF1744, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(evExitFlip,   title="Exit Flip",   style=shape.xcross, location=location.top,    color=#FF9800, size=size.tiny)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DASHBOARD
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_num(_v) =>
    float a = math.abs(_v)
    a >= 1e9 ? str.tostring(_v / 1e9, "#.##") + "B" : a >= 1e6 ? str.tostring(_v / 1e6, "#.##") + "M" : a >= 1e3 ? str.tostring(_v / 1e3, "#.##") + "K" : str.tostring(_v, "#.##")

var table desk = table.new(position.top_right, 2, 8, bgcolor=color.new(#0D1117, 15), border_width=1)

if showTable and barstate.islast
    table.cell(desk, 0, 0, "REGIME", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 0, regime, text_color = alignedBull ? #00C853 : alignedBear ? #FF1744 : divergence ? #AA00FF : #8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 1, "CONVICTION", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 1, str.tostring(score, "#") + " / " + str.tostring(minConviction, "#"), text_color = score >= minConviction ? #00C853 : score <= putThresh ? #FF1744 : #FF9800, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 2, "BIAS", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 2, bias, text_color = callOk or earlyCall ? #00C853 : putOk or earlyPut ? #FF1744 : #8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 3, "HTF FLOW", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 3, not haveHtf ? "Awaiting Data" : htfN > 0 ? "Bull " + str.tostring(htfN, "#.##") : htfN < 0 ? "Bear " + str.tostring(htfN, "#.##") : "Flat", text_color = htfN > 0 ? #00C853 : htfN < 0 ? #FF1744 : #8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 4, "FLOW σ", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 4, str.tostring(strength, "#.##") + "σ  (px " + str.tostring(priceN, "#.##") + ")", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 5, "POSITION", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 5, posDir == 1 ? "LONG @ " + str.tostring(entryPx, format.mintick) : posDir == -1 ? "SHORT @ " + str.tostring(entryPx, format.mintick) : cooldown > 0 ? "Cooldown " + str.tostring(cooldown) : "FLAT", text_color = posDir == 1 ? #00C853 : posDir == -1 ? #FF1744 : #8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 6, "STOP / TARGET", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 6, posDir == 0 ? "—" : str.tostring(stopPx, format.mintick) + " / " + str.tostring(targetPx, format.mintick), text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

    table.cell(desk, 0, 7, "CVD (proxy)", text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(desk, 1, 7, f_num(cvdS), text_color=#8B949E, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_right)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
alertcondition(evEnterLong,  "CALL Entry", "SML CVD Desk → CALL entry")
alertcondition(evEnterShort, "PUT Entry",  "SML CVD Desk → PUT entry")
alertcondition(evExit,       "Exit",       "SML CVD Desk → exit (stop, target or regime flip)")

// ── SqueezeOS webhook bridge — emits the exact JSON /api/webhooks/tradingview
// expects, so entries flow into the IAM executor (Tradier — PAPER by default:
// IAM_PAPER_MODE=true; hard stop-loss orders; daily loss breaker) and the
// Robinhood pending queue. Fires only when a passphrase is configured.
// ENTRIES ONLY, matching every other bridge in indicators/ (SML_DRUCK etc.):
// iam_executor's SELL action means "close any long AND open a bear/put leg",
// not a flat exit, so wiring a target-hit exit to it would silently open a
// fresh un-backtested short on every winning trade. Downside on live longs
// comes from iam_executor's own real stop order (IAM_STOP_LOSS_PCT).
f_whJson(_act) =>
    '{"passphrase":"' + whPass + '","system":"SML_CVD_DESK","ticker":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","action":"' + _act + '","price":' + str.tostring(close, "#.####") + '}'

if barstate.isconfirmed and whPass != ""
    if evEnterLong
        alert(f_whJson("EXECUTE_LONG"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    else if evEnterShort
        alert(f_whJson("EXECUTE_SHORT"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
